      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T15:01:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is your concern with using absl::FunctionRef here exactly? My understanding of absl::FunctionRef is that it exists for this type of situation, eg. you want the caller to provide a function to run as part of function execution and do so in a lightweight and typesafe way. Have you run into problems with FunctionRef in the past?\n\nFWIW it\u0027s possible to make this templated and defined in the source but then pMemoryAndPerformOperation() is a non-member function. It would need an additional parameter to pass in device, hostVisible, lastUsageSerial, memoryAllocation and allocatedSized. I guess could do something with inner class defined in the source file so only the buffer object has to be passed as an extra parameter.",
      "parentUuid": "c20e20d4_e6a43287",
      "revId": "c3968678b4f8de25f0d49279cc76afe8bddc9b4a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
